INTERVIEW TASK 1: API Status Monitor
The Scenario (From your Senior Engineer):
"We have an array of HTTP status codes coming in from the upstream API. I need you to parse it and save only the successful calls—which are 200 and 201—into a separate list. If you see a client error, like a 403 or 404, just skip it and keep processing. But if you hit a 500, that means their server is down. If that happens, halt the entire ingestion process immediately so we don't corrupt our database, and print a critical alert saying the upstream server failed. Print the saved successful calls at the end."

Input Data:

Python
api_logs = [200, 201, 404, 200, 403, 500, 200]

successful_calls = []
for a in api_logs:
    if a == 500:
        print("Critical Alert: Upstream server failed")
        break
    if a == 200 or a == 201:
        successful_calls.append(a)       
print(successful_calls)
